content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-108, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-23110, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal leakage is approximately one drop every two seconds. Leakage at the shaft seal is a documented fault symptom requiring mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check, but the evidence provides no allowable drip-rate or numerical leakage limit, so a numerical pass/fail comparison cannot be made.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is reported as 3.2 mm/s. Figure 3 applies to vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. On that scale, 3.2 mm/s is in Zone B (2.8-4.5 mm/s RMS), labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is below the Zone C threshold of 4.5 mm/s RMS ('Restricted - plan maintenance') and the Zone D threshold of 7.1 mm/s RMS ('Damage likely - stop the pump'). This classification is provisional until RMS units and measurement location are confirmed. Weekly measurements are required on both bearing housings, with the highest reading classified.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature is 68 C. The applicable limits for bearing-housing surface temperature are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. Therefore 68 C is within the normal range and below both the alarm and trip limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No documented immediate-stop condition is established by the supplied readings: vibration is below the 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone D stop threshold and temperature is below the 90 C trip. The active seal leak still requires corrective maintenance; no leak-specific stop threshold is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Investigate early mechanical-seal failure, including worn or cracked seal faces, first. Shaft-seal leakage is associated with worn or cracked faces, and SB-2026-014 documents early failure of component seal HF3-450 on pumps built from serial HF3-22000, caused by a revised sleeve tolerance. P-108's serial HF3-23110 is within that affected range; the actual installed seal and failure mode remain to be confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal dry running is another documented cause of shaft-seal leakage. The HF-300 uses Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry; no evidence in the report confirms whether dry running occurred.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is also a documented cause of shaft-seal leakage and must be checked. The 3.2 mm/s reading alone does not establish misalignment because it falls in Zone B when Figure 3's measurement conditions apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before starting work, verify the pump serial as HF3-23110 and apply SB-2026-014: do not fit component seal HF3-450; obtain cartridge seal HF3-450B and a new casing gasket HF3-120.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before disassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly. Use lifting equipment because its mass is 68 kg. The back pull-out design allows removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the existing seal and shaft sleeve. Inspect the sleeve for scoring and record the scoring depth. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting; this does not eliminate the scoring inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the new HF3-450B cartridge mechanical seal and a new HF3-120 casing gasket. The gasket must be replaced whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten fasteners with lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm, M10 seal gland nuts to 30 Nm for HF3-450B, and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm where disturbed. The 30 Nm gland torque is the service-bulletin override; the other values remain from Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment as part of the seal-leak corrective action. Use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Acceptance tolerances are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to service, ensure the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is available and never run the pump dry. After return to service, continue weekly vibration-velocity measurements on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3; apply the bearing-housing temperature limits of normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; required instead of HF3-450 for this pump because serial HF3-23110 is within the SB-2026-014 affected range. Gland-nut torque is 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; install new whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; conditional replacement part, required if inspection finds scoring deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before removing the back pull-out assembly or working on the seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the documented Plan 11 seal-flush arrangement from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement: standard time 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard time 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal-part conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, while SB-2026-014 prohibits fitting HF3-450 and requires cartridge seal HF3-450B on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward. The bulletin, issued 14 March 2026, applies to P-108 because HF3-23110 is above HF3-22000; use HF3-450B. The manual's HF3-450 instruction remains applicable only to pumps below HF3-22000.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 specifies 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because the bulletin and its cartridge seal apply to this serial, use 30 Nm. Table 5's other fastener torques remain applicable.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the allowable shaft-seal leakage rate and the post-repair leak acceptance criterion? The supplied evidence gives no numerical leak limit or leak-specific shutdown threshold.",
    "Confirm that the reported 3.2 mm/s vibration is an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and provide readings from both drive-end and non-drive-end housings so the highest reading can be classified as required.",
    "Which seal is currently installed, and what do disassembly and inspection show about seal-face wear or cracking, dry running, misalignment and sleeve scoring? The report alone cannot establish the root cause or whether sleeve HF3-455 requires replacement.",
    "What site-specific isolation/lockout, PPE and leaked-fluid handling requirements apply? The supplied maintenance excerpt only states to isolate and drain the pump.",
    "No priority matrix is supplied. P2 is a planning judgement based on the active seal leak while vibration is provisionally Zone B and temperature is normal; confirm the required response time under site rules."
  ]
}
